Subject: [PATCH 4/9] NTimeDiagonalizer: the input seek and the stage code in
 both writers

After an escape, on the tapes off the round's scratch: `qy_seek_run` returns the input head to
1 from any position (the kit's seek on tapes 12 and 13), and `qy_code_calls` computes
`bits (j + 1)` on tape 10 by the increment's and the length call (`j = (unpair s).1`; the code
is its top bit dropped, `stageCode_eq`). `qy_mid_code` and `qy_top_code` host them as the
writers' first phases, ending at the budget's call. The scratch facts: `qy_not_scratch_tp`,
`qy_not_scratch_ge`, `qy_bank_not_scratch`, read through `QyEscT.tp` and `QyEscT.bank`. The
Implementation status paragraph records them.

